e9b1c8543e.001.2"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 31 at 9:50AM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Grand Junction CO has issued a\nFlood Warning for the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nLa Plata River at Hesperus affecting La Plata County.\n\nFor the La Plata River...including Hesperus...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/gjt.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Monday morning at 900 AM MST.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast. This approaches the flood of\nrecord.\n\n* WHERE...La Plata River at Hesperus.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon to Monday morning.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:30 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 4.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage Sunday\nevening to a crest of 5.8 feet late Sunday evening. It will then\nfall below flood stage early Monday morning.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 5.8\nfeet on 05/21/2005.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.516514de7fcd1a54cf04b8b0f74cfdb0cdac2c19.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.516514de7fcd1a54cf04b8b0f74cfdb0cdac2c19.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 30 at 3:02PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and southeast\nUtah, including the following areas, Canyonlands/Natural Bridges,\nLa Sal and Abajo Mountains and Southeast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...From late Saturday night through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recently burned areas, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1 to 3 inches of rain is expected across portions of southeast\nUtah and southwest Colorado from Sunday morning through Monday\nmorning over soils that are still saturated from recent rainfall\nand flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-31T11:37:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 311137 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 537 AM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers continue through Friday night. Lower chances of precipitation Saturday afternoon. - Flooding/flash flooding concerns increase Sunday into Monday, especially for areas that have saturated soils from last week's rain. A Flood Watch remains in effect.","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-31T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-312200- Little Snake Forecast Area- 12